Table Columns <code>artist</code> <code>id</code>, <code>name</code> <code>song</code> <code>id</code>, <code>title</code> <code>artist_song</code> (pivot) <code>id</code>, <code>artist_id</code>, <code>song_id</code> <p>The default pivot table name is the two class names in snake_case, in A-Z order, joined with <code>_</code>. A migration for it:</p> <pre><code>await schema.create('artist_song', (Table table) {
  table.id();
  table.foreignId('artist_id').constrained('artist').cascadeOnDelete();
  table.foreignId('song_id').constrained('song').cascadeOnDelete();
});
</code></pre>

Table Columns <code>photo</code> <code>id</code>, <code>title</code> <code>video</code> <code>id</code>, <code>title</code> <code>comment</code> <code>id</code>, <code>body</code>, <code>commentable_id</code>, <code>commentable_type</code> <p><code>morphs()</code> adds both columns and an index:</p> <pre><code>await schema.create('comment', (Table table) {
