</code></pre>

Field What it is <code>from</code> an <code>Address</code>. Null: <code>MailConfig.from</code> <code>to</code>, <code>cc</code>, <code>bcc</code> lists of <code>Address</code> <code>replyTo</code> a list of <code>Address</code> <code>subject</code> text <code>text</code> the plain text body <code>html</code> the HTML body <code>attachments</code> a list of <code>Attachment</code> <code>headers</code> more headers, like <code>{'X-Campaign': 'fall'}</code> <code>tags</code> tags for the reports of the provider. See Tags and metadata <code>metadata</code> key and value data for the provider, like <code>{'user_id': '42'}</code> <p>A subject or header with a line break is an error, so user input cannot add headers.</p> <p>An <code>Address</code> is an email and an optional name. <code>Address.parse</code> reads one from text, and <code>Address.list</code> reads many:</p> <pre><code>Address('ann@example.com', 'Ann');
Address.parse('Ann &lt;ann@example.com&gt;');
Address.list(&lt;String&gt;['ann@example.com', 'bob@example.com']);
</code></pre>

Callback Runs <code>before(job)</code> one time, at <code>dispatch()</code>, before the jobs are pushed <code>progress(job)</code> each time a job is done. With <code>allowFailures()</code>, also when one fails <code>then(job)</code> one time, when every job is done <code>catchError(job)</code> one time, when the first job fails for good <code>whenComplete(job)</code> one time, when every job ran, done or failed <p>Each callback is a job. It runs one time, with no retry. Add <code>Batchable</code> to read the batch, and <code>CatchesError</code> to read the error:</p> <pre><code>@Job()
class ImportFailed extends DoxJob with Batchable, CatchesError {
  @override
  Future&lt;void&gt; handle() async {
    Batch? batch = await this.batch();
    await alertAdmin('import ${batch?.name} failed: $caughtError');
  }
}
</code></pre>

Option What it sets <code>font</code> The fonts, by name. See Using other fonts. <code>colorType</code> <code>ColorType.rgb</code> (default) or <code>ColorType.cmyk</code>. <code>lang</code> The PDF language and the default date locale, like <code>en</code>. <code>title</code>, <code>author</code>, <code>subject</code>, <code>keywords</code>, <code>creator</code>, <code>producer</code> The PDF metadata. <code>creationDate</code>, <code>modificationDate</code> The PDF dates. <p>Read the pdfme options JSON with <code>GenerateOptions.fromJson</code>:</p> <pre><code>GenerateOptions options =
    GenerateOptions.fromJson(&lt;String, Object?&gt;{'lang': 'en'});
</code></pre>

Field Type Default Meaning <code>defaultStore</code> <code>String</code> required The store <code>Cache()</code> uses when no store is named. <code>stores</code> <code>Map&lt;String, Map&lt;String, dynamic&gt;&gt;</code> required Store name to options. Each store needs a <code>driver</code> option. <code>flags</code> <code>CacheFlags</code> <code>CacheFlags()</code> (all off) Opt-in cache behaviors. See below. <code>encrypter</code> <code>CacheEncrypter?</code> <code>null</code> Encrypts stores with <code>'encrypt': true</code>. Dox sets it. You need it only without Dox. <p><code>CacheFlags</code> has one flag. <code>CacheFlags.all()</code> turns it on.</p> Flag When it is on <code>lockThrows</code> <code>lock.block(timeout)</code> with no callback throws <code>LockTimeoutException</code> when the lock was not taken in time. Off: it gives <code>false</code>. Set <code>lock.throwOnTimeout</code> to pick for one lock. <pre><code>CacheConfig(
  defaultStore: 'redis',
  stores: stores,
  flags: const CacheFlags(lockThrows: true),
);
</code></pre> <p>Options of each driver:</p> Driver Option Type Default Meaning all <code>driver</code> <code>String</code> required <code>file</code>, <code>memory</code>, <code>redis</code>, <code>database</code> or <code>null</code> all <code>prefix</code> <code>String</code> <code>dox_cache:</code> (<code>&lt;app name&gt;_cache:</code> on Redis) Text in front of each key. <code>file</code>, <code>redis</code>, <code>database</code> <code>encrypt</code> <code>bool</code> <code>false</code> Encrypt the values with the app key. <code>file</code> <code>path</code> <code>String</code> <code>storage/cache</code> Folder of the cache files. <code>file</code> <code>prune_every</code> <code>int</code> <code>0</code> Run <code>prune()</code> once every this many writes. <code>0</code>: a light prune at most once an hour. <code>file</code> <code>fsync</code> <code>bool</code> <code>true</code> Sync each write to the disk. <code>false</code> is faster, but a power cut can lose the last writes. <code>memory</code> <code>max_size</code> <code>int</code> no limit Most items in the map. <code>redis</code> <code>host</code> <code>String</code> <code>127.0.0.1</code> Redis host. <code>redis</code> <code>port</code> <code>int</code> <code>6379</code> Redis port. <code>redis</code> <code>username</code> <code>String</code> none Redis user. <code>redis</code> <code>password</code> <code>String</code> none Redis password. <code>redis</code> <code>db</code> <code>int</code> <code>0</code> Redis database number. <code>redis</code> <code>tls</code> <code>bool</code> <code>false</code> Use TLS. <code>redis</code> <code>pool_size</code> <code>int</code> <code>10</code> Most connections per store. <code>redis</code> <code>max_value_bytes</code> <code>int</code> no limit Biggest value in bytes. <code>redis</code> <code>options</code> <code>RedisOptions</code> none All client options. See Redis options. <code>database</code> <code>table</code>, <code>connection</code>, <code>prune_interval</code> See Database store.

Code Gives <code>await req.validate&lt;CreateBlog&gt;()</code> checked DTO, or <code>422</code> <code>req.input('name')</code> one value, query or body (body wins) <code>req.all()</code> / <code>req.only(&lt;String&gt;['a', 'b'])</code> many values <code>req.input('user.name', 'guest')</code> dot key, with a default <code>req.except(&lt;String&gt;['password'])</code> all values but these <code>req.has('name')</code> / <code>req.filled('name')</code> key is there and not empty (only <code>filled</code> reads dot keys) <code>req.exists('name')</code> / <code>req.missing('name')</code> key is there (any value) / not there <code>req.boolean('remember')</code> / <code>req.integer('page', 1)</code> value as <code>bool</code> / <code>int</code> <code>req.file('avatar')</code> / <code>req.hasFile('avatar')</code> uploaded file <code>req.bearerToken()</code> token of <code>Authorization: Bearer</code> <code>req.path()</code> / <code>req.fullUrl()</code> path / full URL with query <code>req.pathIs('admin/*')</code> / <code>req.routeIs('admin.*')</code> path or route name matches <code>req.body</code> / <code>req.query</code> / <code>req.param['id']</code> one source only <code>req.header('X-Token')</code> / <code>req.headers</code> headers <code>req.cookie('token')</code> decrypted cookie <code>req.ip()</code> / <code>req.scheme()</code> / <code>req.isSecure()</code> client info. Needs <code>trustedProxies</code> behind a proxy. <code>req.userAgent()</code> / <code>req.host()</code> / <code>req.origin()</code> / <code>req.locale</code> more headers <code>req.isJson()</code> / <code>req.isFormData()</code> content type <code>req.auth?.user&lt;User&gt;()</code> logged in user (after <code>AuthMiddleware</code>) <code>req.auth?.id()</code> / <code>req.auth == null</code> user id, or <code>true</code> for a guest <code>req.method</code> / <code>req.uri</code> method and URI <p>Files:</p> <pre><code>RequestFile file = req.input('avatar');
file.filename; file.extension; file.length;   // bytes
// save before you return (dox_storage)
String path = await file.store('avatars');
</code></pre> <p>See Request and Request and response.</p>
